* Question: how much external TLS still negotiates classical-only key
* agreement, and how much already negotiates a hybrid group?
*
* This is one search, not two, because the numerator and the denominator have
* to come from the same filter or the ratio is meaningless. Splitting them into
* separate saved searches is the most common way this metric goes wrong.
*
* Source: Zeek/Corelight ssl.log via the Splunk_TA_zeek or Corelight TA.
* Adjust index and sourcetype to the local deployment.
*
* Not an alert. Schedule daily, feed a dashboard or summary index. Routing this
* to an analyst queue is a deployment error.
*
* Validation status: [inference] - field names from Zeek documentation, not
* verified against a live indexer. See detection/README.md.

index=zeek sourcetype=zeek:ssl earliest=-1d@d latest=@d
| eval curve=coalesce(curve, cipher_suite_curve, "unknown")
| eval group_class=case(
    match(curve, "(?i)mlkem|kyber|x25519mlkem|secp256r1mlkem|4588|11ec"), "hybrid_pqc",
    match(curve, "(?i)^(x25519|secp256r1|secp384r1|secp521r1|ffdhe)"), "classical_only",
    curve=="unknown", "unobserved",
    1==1, "other")
| stats count AS sessions,
        dc(id.resp_h) AS distinct_servers BY group_class, server_name
| eventstats sum(sessions) AS total_sessions
| eval pct_of_total=round(100*sessions/total_sessions, 2)
| table group_class server_name sessions distinct_servers pct_of_total
| sort - sessions
